00:12:27.863 --> 00:12:29.894
- [Mark] You must feel lucky to be alive.

00:12:29.894 --> 00:12:31.150
- That'd be the lucky.

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:32.497
I feel like,

00:12:32.497 --> 00:12:34.207
(train horns)

00:12:34.207 --> 00:12:37.710
I feel like, it's kind
of part of my life now.

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:38.753
So I was like, okay.

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:43.830
Yeah. And you still have to
take medication, you know

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:45.870
you go in and out of things

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:47.660
and then things happen.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:48.493
And am here.

00:12:48.493 --> 00:12:51.973
- [Mark] So what, what are you
doing today with your life?

00:12:51.973 --> 00:12:53.290
- What am I doing now?

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:54.940
- [Mark] Yeah. Where do you live?

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:56.830
- I'm homeless.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:58.070
- [Mark] You're homeless.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:12:59.270
You're here on Skid Row?

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:04.090
- I guess everywhere downtown
is almost considered Skid Row

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:07.454
but I, yeah, I come
and eat at the mission.

00:13:07.454 --> 00:13:09.810
- [Mark] You live in a tent?

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.490
- No, I'm more of a train sleeper.

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:14.010
I like to be on the train.

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:15.830
I don't feel safe down here.

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:16.933
I get bullied.

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:21.020
Yeah. I don't really fit in down here.

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:23.330
- [Mark] So you're riding train all night?

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:24.450
- Yeah.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:25.460
Yeah.

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:28.040
Which that is good that they
actually keep the train running

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:29.670
for homeless people.

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:31.860
But yeah, I, I came back out here

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:34.760
because of the fact that I lost my place

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:37.363
and I was so happy to have a place.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.720
Cause you know, a lot I've
happened after losing my aunt

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:42.230
but that's neither here or there.

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:44.550
But I'm homeless and

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.550
I don't live in a tent.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:47.903
I don't really like tents.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:53.414
I like to be in doors with, you know

00:13:53.414 --> 00:13:55.970
walls and the door and all that.

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:58.700
And I don't wanna get
too complacent with that.

00:13:58.700 --> 00:13:59.609
But,

00:13:59.609 --> 00:14:01.523
- [Mark] And do you use any
drugs that are on the street?

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:04.130
- Yeah,

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:04.963
I do.

00:14:04.963 --> 00:14:05.940
- [Mark] Which ones?

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:08.028
- The popular crystal meth.

00:14:08.028 --> 00:14:10.150
- [Mark] Crystal meth is popular I know.

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:11.750
- Yeah,

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:12.600
I do.

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:15.543
But I guess you could say
I was doing that before.

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:19.300
It didn't have anything to do
with me actually coming back

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:20.790
to Skid row.

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.640
But I've been doing crystal meth

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:23.973
because I consider myself,

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:27.143
not gay,

00:14:27.143 --> 00:14:30.410
but I, I have intercourse with males.

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:33.080
So that was, you know, that
was a gay drug at first

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:37.380
and then it hit here and
now it's really an epidemic

00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:40.423
but yeah, I am currently
doing crystal meth.

00:14:42.991 --> 00:14:45.120
- [Mark] And what, do you have any plans?

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:47.490
I mean what, you're kind
of stuck here in Skid row

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.980
doing drugs and it's like,
it's got that the most.

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:53.040
- Plans, well my plan fell through.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.322
I had a place.

00:14:54.322 --> 00:14:56.540
And it's almost, it hasn't
even been a year yet

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.800
but I ain't got a place DMH

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:02.410
and I have to relinquish my unit

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:03.853
because I was being bullied.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:06.611
I'm being bullied again.

00:15:06.611 --> 00:15:07.780
(laughs)

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:09.150
So I'm used to being bullied

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:12.610
because right before coming to the Roslyn

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:14.910
or what have you, the DMH.

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:17.230
I was at a transitional home.

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:19.303
I was bullied there by all the men.

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:22.610
I mean, they were taking my clothes.

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:24.850
I mean, I was calling my
mom every day, saying there,

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:26.380
this, this is happening, that's happening.

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:28.230
And I was just always,
everywhere that I go

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:31.840
I'm always kind of by
myself, even if I'm popular

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:35.180
but people won't like me for no reason.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:38.060
So I think I'm just, I'm
expected for that set.

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:39.960
I expect that to happen now

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:42.040
but it's really gotten physical.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.630
Like me getting hit.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:44.463
I got hit.

00:15:44.463 --> 00:15:46.910
I've been hit on a train, for no reason.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:49.340
I've had a knife put out
on me, for no reason.

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:52.180
I'm asleep, I wake up
and a guy has a knife

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:53.620
because he's tweaking.

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:54.453
I am,

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.280
no actually he suck me in my eye

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:00.410
and you know you're asleep.

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:01.243
Who?

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:05.540
That's almost like, okay,
did I get sucked out of life?

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:06.440
It feels weird.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.700
I didn't know what happened.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:11.350
Then he had a weapon
which was a knife ,out of

00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:13.500
I don't know why I'm the only,

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.940
It seems like I'm the only one downtown

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:17.613
that gets bullied as much.

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:19.800
Yeah.

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:22.260
I can be with other people
and they won't say anything

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:25.240
to them, but they will
say something to me.

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:28.473
But I guess it's, that's what happens.

00:16:28.473 --> 00:16:32.050
So I'm here now and it's not that bad.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:33.250
It's this Turner.

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:35.400
I mean, this come around
well I guess this,

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:39.090
second time being homeless.

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:41.373
I don't, I find clothes
and things like that.

00:16:42.717 --> 00:16:45.940
I've always been into
clothes and things but,

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:48.180
it's not that bad now I
know how to handle it.

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:52.515
And, I have these puppies,
puppies on a leash now, so yeah.

00:16:52.515 --> 00:16:53.687
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:16:53.687 --> 00:16:54.520
- I'm good.

00:16:54.520 --> 00:16:55.447
- [Mark] All right.

00:16:55.447 --> 00:16:56.280
Well Brandon, thank you.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.320
- [Brandon] Thank you.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:58.153
- [Mark] For sharing your story

00:16:58.153 --> 00:17:00.414
and good luck with
wherever you go from here.

00:17:00.414 --> 00:17:01.247
- [Brandon] Thank you.

00:17:01.247 --> 00:17:02.080
- [Mark] All right. Thank you.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.913
- [Brandon] All right.

